{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3424","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3424","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3424\",\"parent_revision\":\"48c8153d58bc128a8f5b5ae3df55d7a8090888a80a5da7dfca3ec29ffd3194a3\",\"root_revision\":\"48c8153d58bc128a8f5b5ae3df55d7a8090888a80a5da7dfca3ec29ffd3194a3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe orchestrator that drives dh has no file of its own. It is the main session running `dh:dispatch`, `dh:implement-feature`, and `dh:groom-milestone`; there is no `orchestrator.md` among the 29 agent definitions. Its interface is the skill prose it reads and the tokens it branches on.\\n\\nIt makes four decisions per step:\\n1. Did this step succeed? \u2014 reads the worker's STATUS first line\\n2. Should the task be marked done? \u2014 the SubagentStop hook writes task state\\n3. Which step is next? \u2014 the stage-to-gate map\\n4. What did the step produce? \u2014 an artifact handle passed to the next agent\\n\\nDecisions 1 and 3 are described in dh skill prose, and 1 is almost line for line the Adjudicate section of the consolidated `agent-orchestration:delegate` skill. Two plugins currently describe the same decision loop.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: the loop drifts in two places independently. A change to adjudication in agent-orchestration does not reach dh, and dh's copy silently disagrees \u2014 which is how the STATUS vocabulary forked in the first place (see #3423).\\n\\nProposal for grooming, not a decided design: dh dispatch skills reference `agent-orchestration:delegate` for the decision loop and retain only the SAM-specific bindings \u2014 which status enum, which hook writes task state, which artifact operation stores output. dh grows no orchestrator document of its own.\\n\\nConstraint from the pinned decisions: gates go on outcomes, never on dispatch prompt shape. PR #3422 deletes the repo-level validate-delegation hook, and dh must not add a prompt-shape gate to replace it. Any convergence here is about where the decision loop is documented, not about validating prompt structure.\\n\\nSequencing: blocked on agent-orchestration PR #3422 merging, which establishes `delegate` as the single ad-hoc template and `parallel-work` as the fan-out reference.\\n\\nUser-provided context: identified as the convergence point between the dh and agent-orchestration packages that neither plan currently names.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: DH delegation-spine audit, session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"109be45022573d73bd4a5094f6f8950b044c000464824b7323f1a77f67235778\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSzTQkA\"}"}